# Shell scripts run inside Linux containers: always LF line endings, even
# on a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf would otherwise turn them into CRLF
# and `sh` would fail with "not found").
*.sh text eol=lf

# Migrations: always LF too. SQLx checksums each migration's exact bytes, so
# a CRLF checkout would make every database that ran it refuse to start
# ("migration N was previously applied but has been modified").
*.sql text eol=lf
